# CUSTOM
# Python bytecode. The repository ships rig tooling and test harnesses as
# modules, so any run of them -- or a py_compile syntax check -- leaves these
# beside the sources.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Artifacts the documented workflows drop at the worktree root. The Win32
# verification procedure has you write a .bat beside the sources and run the
# test binary from the worktree root, where LrpkGoldenBytesTests writes
# golden.lrpk through a relative path. Both accumulated as untracked litter on
# the retiring rig; ignoring them is cheaper than remembering to delete them.
# Anchored, because only the root is where the procedure puts them: a helper
# script under scripts/ or a fixture under tests/ must stay visible.
/*.bat
/golden.lrpk

# Local planning notes and session handoffs (Japanese, machine-specific paths).
# The handoff skill relies on this being ignored in every clone, not just ones
# with a hand-edited .git/info/exclude.
/plans/
/agent/pilot.md
**/build
compile_commands.json
CMakeUserPresets.json
.env-retro68
.env-mame
.env-mame-*

